Thursday Update -- Correction
* Trade Alert: Correction on strike, date and lmt price of Deere calls--Sto=
cks are rising and the dollar strengthening after initial jobless claims fe=
ll to the lowest level since the end of November, beating market expectatio=
ns.Through midday, the Dow climbed by 249.33 points, or 0.8%, to 30,972.11,=
 with S&amp;P 500 higher by 0.8% to 3,859.04 points and Nasdaq up by 0.8% t=
o 13,718.24 points. The financials sector was the standout performer follow=
ed by health care and utilities.Initial jobless claims fell to 779,000 duri=
ng the week ended Jan. 30 from 812,000 a week ago, beneath the consensus fo=
r 835,000. The four-week moving average dropped to 848,250, breaking the st=
ring of recent increases as early January spikes work their way out of the =
equation. Continuing claims slid by 193,000 to 4,592,000 in the week ended =
Jan. 23."The third consecutive week of decline, while still elevated, the o=
ngoing improvement in claims suggests layoffs have slowed, a positive sign =
for the labor market as well as the broad-based recovery effort," Stifel Ch=
ief Economist Lindsey Piegza said in a report. "Steps in the right directio=
n are encouraging that the US economy could and will eventually return to a=
 stronger jobs position amid a widespread vaccination effort to contain the=
 virus."Citing data from the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, UB=
S said in a research note that vaccination rate has risen in the US and at =
the current pace the country is on "track to reach herd immunity in late Ju=
ne." As per the CDC, the herd immunity threshold for SARS-CoV-2, the virus =
that causes COVID-19, is expected to range between 50% and 65%, the note sa=
id.Meanwhile, new orders for US factory goods rose by 1.1% in December, abo=
ve expectations for a 0.7% increase in an Econoday survey and following an =
upwardly revised 1.3% increase in November.In company news, shares of Align=
 Technology (ALGN) surged more than 14% intraday, the most on S&amp;P 500 a=
nd Nasdaq, after fourth-quarter sales and earnings beat the market expectat=
ions. On both the indexes, the steepest decliner was Qualcomm (QCOM), after=
 the company reported fiscal first quarter sales that missed guidance, send=
ing shares down by 9% even though earnings beat forecast.L Brands (LB) was =
the second-highest gainer on S&amp;P 500 after the company raised earnings =
guidance for the fourth quarter. The company said Stuart Burgdoerfer is pla=
nning to retire as chief financial officer and step down as interim chief e=
xecutive of Victoria's Secret business. Shares jumped by 10%.In the metals =
markets, silver was down 2.6% to $26.20 an ounce and copper was down 0.5% t=
o $3.55 per pound..Portfolio: We came into today with no positions and now =
have one recommendation. ... Please note below the corrected strike, date a=
nd symbol of the Deere calls. ... Sorry for the inconvenience.*NEW RECOMMEN=
DATIONDeere and Co. (DE)&nbsp;&nbsp;February 310 calls-- Symbol:&nbsp;&nbsp=
;DE210219C00310000-- Order: Buy at $7.50 lmt day only-- If filled, set up t=
o sell half at $10.75 lmt gtc and half at $12.75 lmt gtc-- If filled, set s=
top at $5.25 stp, good after 10:30 a.m. ET only*Jon D. MarkmanAll recommend=
ations are for monthly options expiring on the third Friday of the specifie=
d month unless otherwise noted. All stops are good after 10:30 a.m. Eastern=
 only unless otherwise specified. All orders are good for the day only unle=
ss otherwise noted. "Day only" orders expire at the close of the current se=
ssion. Past results are no guarantee of future returns. All accounts may no=
t achieve comparable results. Recommendations are leveraged and speculative=
, so only use risk capital =E2=80=94 i.e., money you can afford to lose. Al=
l results are shown ex-commissions and fees. Options trading involves the r=
isk of substantial loss. Some news and research provided by Wall Street Jou=
rnal, Bloomberg, Associated Press, MT Newswires and Reuters.&nbsp;

